# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this React + Vite project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package (v2.0.0) using npm
- Package added to dependencies in `package.json`
- Lock file (`package-lock.json`) updated with new dependency

### 2. Code Integration
**Modified: `frontend/src/App.tsx`**
- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react';`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component alongside the existing `<Analytics />` component
- Component placed inside the main app container, following React best practices

## Implementation Details

### Framework Detection
This project uses:
- **Framework**: React 18.3.0
- **Build Tool**: Vite 5.4.0
- **Package Manager**: npm

### Documentation Reference
Implementation followed the official Vercel Speed Insights Quickstart guide (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), specifically the React/Create React App instructions:
- Used the `/react` entry point for the SpeedInsights import
- Added the component to the root App component for global coverage

### Placement Rationale
The SpeedInsights component was placed:
- At the root level of the application (App.tsx)
- Next to the existing Analytics component for consistency
- Inside the main BrowserRouter wrapper to track all route changes

## Verification

✅ **Build Test**: Successfully ran `npm run build` - project compiles without errors
✅ **Package Installation**: Confirmed `@vercel/speed-insights` added to package.json dependencies
✅ **Lock File**: package-lock.json updated with 291 new packages (transitive dependencies)
✅ **Code Integration**: SpeedInsights component properly imported and rendered

## Next Steps

Once deployed to Vercel, Speed Insights will:
1. Automatically track Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS, FCP, TTFB, INP)
2. Collect real user monitoring data
3. Display performance metrics in the Vercel dashboard under Speed Insights section

No additional configuration is required. The component will work seamlessly with the existing Vercel Analytics setup.
